{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions","id":1027389,"title":"Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-05T19:56:20-08:00","id":1027389,"title":"Conditions","content":"Conditions are present since GMC rules update, and they are one of the core parts of CoD. I don't think they are going to be less important in near future, actually I see the opposite trend. What's more conditions are (next to aspirations) main source of EXP for player characters. Everything fine so far. I understand it, I see potential in it, I explain it to my players but they still see it as a necessary evil. They avoid conditions at all cost, they don't want to solve them (even a positive condition sticks with a PC four couple of games until it fades down with the end of the story) and by all means they avoid resolving conditions that can actually harm them (such as spooked, shaken, etc.) Is it just me and my players or do you have similar problems? What do you guys think I could do make players use the conditions more as the game intends to?<br /> <br /> Side note: Funny thing is that my players don't usually have problems with putting their characters into troubles or failing rolls to make story more interesting. We play a lot of L5R, WFRP 3ed, and some FATE-based games and they never had this kind of problems, until the conditions in CoD appeared :|.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:19:15-08:00","id":1027398,"title":"","content":"You could point out that not all Conditions involve putting them into trouble.<br /> <br /> If they're less interested in a story and more in just character advancement you could just remove them. You could replace them with 'Effects' and instead of offering advantages or disadvantages and ways to gain Beats, they can just offer advantages and disadvantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:23:08-08:00","id":1027399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027398#post1027398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could point out that not all Conditions involve putting them into trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tehy are equally reluctant towards positive conditions. Actually any conditions at all. They just keep complaining that they get tons of conditions that have no sense whatsoever and don't do enything with them. I find it strange but IMO there must be some knowledge/communication problem in it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:32:51-08:00","id":1027402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027399#post1027399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tehy are equally reluctant towards positive conditions. Actually any conditions at all. They just keep complaining that they get tons of conditions that have no sense whatsoever and don't do enything with them. I find it strange but IMO there must be some knowledge/communication problem in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, then. Conditions are the same as effects. Someone casts charm on you, you're charmed. You chop someone up with an axe, you're blood-drenched, -3 to social rolls involving your appearance. All Conditions do is give you a way to get Experience by playing it up.<br /> <br /> This has come up before, but I don't really 'get' the issue people have with it. Are you using Condition Cards or anything? Or just telling them they have the 'blank' Condition and letting them do the rest? When they had something happen to them before, did they just ignore it? Like if their character was blinded they just acted like they could see and didn't use whatever penalty to their dice rolls it caused?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:33:04-08:00","id":1027403,"title":"","content":"Have you tried pointing out that Conditions aren't anything new? They're no different than any of the other various floating modifiers from 1e. They just have names now, and you get exp for roleplaying them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:59:06-08:00","id":1027412,"title":"","content":"I can only suggest taking a cue from Werewolf, Beast, or Demon, all of which have specific Conditions involved as a regular facet of being a member of that splat \u2014 Werewolf slightly less so, but Beast and Demon both have &quot;you will always at least start a session with a Persistent Condition&quot; baked into the template.<br /> <br /> Is this problem occurring across multiple games or is it just exhibiting itself within a single ongoing chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:01:07-08:00","id":1027414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027412#post1027412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can only suggest taking a cue from Werewolf, Beast, or Demon, all of which have specific Conditions involved as a regular facet of being a member of that splat \u2014 Werewolf slightly less so, but Beast and Demon both have &quot;you will always at least start a session with a Persistent Condition&quot; baked into the template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you expand? I'm not very familiar with neither.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027412#post1027412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this problem occurring across multiple games or is it just exhibiting itself within a single ongoing chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like ongoing. I had it during werewolf chronicle, in some on-off games, and now I'm having it again in my Mage chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:18:13-08:00","id":1027420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027414#post1027414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you expand? I'm not very familiar with neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast has a set of Persistent Conditions that you move between depending on where you are on the Integrity-bar equivalent \u2014 you explicitly always have one, since the Resolution criterion for each one involves the acquisition criterion for another \u2014 and while the Agenda Conditions of Demon aren't explicitly Persistent Conditions except for Uncalled (which is the &quot;not having an Agenda is rough sometimes&quot; counterpart to the proper Agenda Conditions), every Agenda effectively gives you its own variant of Connected (get a Beat once per session for hitting particular story beats, Resolve the Condition at will for a decent bonus) that renews itself at the start of each game session, and there's Merits that give you a second Agenda or allow you to Resolve an Agenda Condition twice per chapter instead of once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:30:31-08:00","id":1027429,"title":"","content":"I'll have to take a look at them. I'm wondering how that would work with Mage, though and how to make my players start resolving conditions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T21:48:56-08:00","id":1027448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027389-conditions?p=1027429#post1027429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to take a look at them. I'm wondering how that would work with Mage, though and how to make my players start resolving conditions...</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul loss is a pretty solid motivator, if you have room in the narrative for it.<br /> <br /> Alternately, make ample use of the fact that mages frequently inflict Conditions on themselves to grow faster \u2014 make NPC mages who engage in this practice in some form notably stronger than NPC mages who don't undertake these sorts of self-imposed/mentor-mandated challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T22:25:41-08:00","id":1027461,"title":"","content":"Have you asked your players why they don't like Conditions? I think it would be easier to recommend solutions if we had a better idea what the problem is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T23:47:36-08:00","id":1027472,"title":"","content":"Instead of using generic conditions, try to craft specific conditions that apply to a specific situation and character. This should remove their argument of making no sense (as you made sure that it makes sense, and is a direct continuation of their actions) and also look really cool. We sold Conditions to one of our new players by giving her a Condition for spending a scene dressing up and making sure everything is perfect for her meeting with important NPC, and she loved it. A condition card is a cool achievment-like reminder of your actions, too.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, instead of just dice modifiers, make resolving a Condition lead into some narrative effect. This way, they will have to resolve conditions to actually do stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-06-2017, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}